(7413911, 1168630, 94815, '<td valign="top">Lusciously ambiguous. I think there are tasty meats in there and some shoppers but not too sure. The hog, living or dead, is clearly disdainful of it all. 7</td>', 'Lusciously ambiguous. I think there are tasty meats in there and some shoppers but not too sure. The hog, living or dead, is clearly disdainful of it all. 7', '2015-11-03 16:02:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7413912, 1168491, 38032, '<td valign="top">Love the almost-eye-contact from many of these people. Really nice to explore.<br/>Coming back for another look - you have captured humanity''s seriousness, silliness, and ironies. The ladder remains an odd bit which is just one of the things to wonder in this great composition. The 2-half-shirt, the ORIGINAL shirt, the signage, the mere crowdedness and meaninglessness of it all. Wonderful. <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1167384" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1167384.png'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1167384.png'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1167384.png"/></a> Bumping to 9.</td>', 'Love the almost-eye-contact from many of these people. Really nice to explore.Coming back for another look - you have captured humanity''s seriousness, silliness, and ironies. The ladder remains an odd bit which is just one of the things to wonder in this great composition. The 2-half-shirt, the ORIGINAL shirt, the signage, the mere crowdedness and meaninglessness of it all. Wonderful.  Bumping to 9.', '2015-11-03 16:32:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7413913, 1168827, 38032, '<td valign="top">What is it about this that keeps me looking back at this one?  I don''t know. Maybe I never will.  It is the linear game being played  in the composition? Is the ghosts that were here and left nothing but footprints? The image prevails and leaves me wondering  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1167385" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1167385.png'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1167385.png'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1167385.png"/></a></td>', 'What is it about this that keeps me looking back at this one?  I don''t know. Maybe I never will.  It is the linear game being played  in the composition? Is the ghosts that were here and left nothing but footprints? The image prevails and leaves me wondering  ', '2015-11-03 16:38:17.000000', NULL, 1);
